237	185,870,681,1351	237. Flower of Pennsylvanian Anemony.	An open Anemony flower seen from above, five broad veined sepals spread round a dense tuft of many stamens, on a short stalk.
238	776,927,1491,1356	238. Half a flower of a Crowfoot, magnified.	A Crowfoot flower cut down the middle: broad veined petals, a ring of many stamens, and the pistils crowded on the raised receptacle above the stalk.
239	1627,824,1752,994	239. A petal, showing its little scale.	A single Crowfoot petal, rounded at the top and narrowed to the base, with a tiny scale drawn just above its claw.
240	181,1400,304,1706	240. Pod of Marsh-Marigold, opening.	A curved, pointed pod of the Marsh-Marigold split open along one side, showing a row of seeds inside.
241	373,1398,494,1713	241. A pistil of Anemony, magnified, the ovary cut through to show the ovule in it.	A single Anemony pistil with a long curved style, its swollen ovary cut open to show the one ovule within.
242	566,1422,766,1714	242. Akene of Crowfoot, enlarged.	A flattened, rounded Crowfoot akene finely lined over its surface and ending in a short hooked beak.
243	848,1427,1048,1712	243. Same, cut through to show the seed in it.	The Crowfoot akene cut through, its thin wall enclosing the single rounded seed, with the hooked beak at the top.
244	1110,1496,1331,1709	244. Enlarged cross-section of the sepals of Virgin's-Bower No. 1, in the bud.	A cross-section of a Virgin's-Bower bud: four sepals meeting edge to edge in a lobed ring, their edges turned slightly inward.
245	1356,1514,1577,1710	245. Same of Virgin's-Bower No. 3.	A cross-section of another Virgin's-Bower bud, the edges of its sepals rolled inward into small curls round the ring.
246	1601,1067,1756,1706	246. Akene and feathery tail or style of Virgin's-Bower No. 1.	A small dark pointed akene at the foot of a long, plumy style, feathered with fine hairs along its whole length.
